his, to day is the third day since these things were done.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaYea, and certain women also of our company made us astonished, which were early at the sepulchre;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~and when they found not his body, they came, saying, that they had also seen a vision of angels, which said that he was alive.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd certain of them which were with us went to the sepulchre, and found it even so as the women had said: but him they saw not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Then he said unto them, O fools, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLought not Christ to have suffered these things, and to enter into his glory?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd beginning at Moses and all the prophets, he expounded unto them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiAnd they drew nigh unto the village, whither they went: and he made as though he would have gone further.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡But they constrained him, saying, Abide with us: for it is toward evening, and the day is far spent. And he went in to tarry with them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd it came to pass, as he sat at meat with them, he took bread, and blessed it, and brake, and gave to them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd their eyes were opened, and they knew him; and he vanished out of their sight.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they said one to another, Did not our heart burn within us, while he talked with us by the way, and while he opened to us the scriptures?¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And they rose up the same hour, and returned to Jerusalem, and found the eleven gathered together, and them that were with them,¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=saying, The Lord is risen indeed, and hath appeared to Simon.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd they told what things were done in the way, and how he was known of them in breaking of bread.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book)§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse+¦verses˜„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiAnd as they thus spake, Jesus himself stood in the midst of them, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQBut they were terrified and affrighted, and supposed that they had seen a spirit.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd he said unto them, Why are ye troubled? and why do thoughts arise in your hearts?¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBehold my hands and my feet, that it is I myself: handle me, and see; for a spirit hath not flesh and bones, as ye see me have.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd when he had thus spoken, he shewed them his hands and his feet.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And while they yet believed not for joy, and wondered, he said unto them, Have ye here any meat?¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAAnd they gave him a piece of a broiled fish, and of an honeycomb.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ(And he took it, and did eat before them.¦layout ªlast_verse+…¤book)§chapter«first_verse,ªlast_verse1¦verses–„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŞAnd he said unto them, These are the words which I spake unto you, while I was yet with you, that all things must be fulfilled, which were written in the law of Moses, and in the prophets, and in the psalms, concerning me.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNThen opened he their understanding, that they might understand the scriptures,¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvand said unto them, Thus it is written, and thus it behoved Christ to suffer, and to rise from the dead the third day:¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsand that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in his name among all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ%And ye are witnesses of these things.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And, behold, I send the promise of my Father upon you: but tarry ye in the city of Jerusalem, until ye be endued with power from on high.¦layout ªlast_verse1…¤book)§chapter«first_verse2ªlast_verse5¦verses”„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd he led them out as far as to Bethany, and he lifted up his hands, and blessed them.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And it came to pass, while he blessed them, he was parted from them, and carried up into heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBAnd they worshipped him, and returned to Jerusalem with great joy:¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDand were continually in the temple, praising and blessing God. Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse5